    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0210" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/7048</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-31T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1253. Your 3059, October 29, 4 p.m. Department can not sanction any activities,
                    however urgent and distressing the need, which require cooperation or patronage
                    of Bolshevik authorities. Has so advised Red Cross here and Ambassador at
                    Archangel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
